course: dictionary
lesson: 1939
title: Commentators: who describes and who gives opinions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A commentator is someone who tells you about an event, either as it happens or by giving their view on it. Sports commentators describe the match on TV, radio or online, moment by moment.
explain: Some commentators write or speak about the news and say what they think. «A news report tells what happened; an opinion piece or commentator says what someone thinks about it.» The news report gives the facts, and the commentator gives the opinion.
explain: Use the words around commentator as clues. A "football commentator" talks about football, and a "political commentator" talks about politics. The word before commentator tells you the topic.
fact: A commentator is a person who describes events or gives opinions on them.
fact: A sports commentator describes a match as it happens, on TV, radio or online.
fact: A political commentator writes or speaks about politics and gives opinions on it.
fact: «Running commentary» means a description given while the action is still going on.
fact: A news report says what happened; a commentator says what they think about it.
exercise: «A news report tells what happened; an opinion piece or commentator says what someone thinks about it.» What does a commentator do? | Only lists facts with no opinion | Runs the sports field | Cooks food on the radio | *Gives opinions about events and news
exercise: A football commentator on the radio shouts, «He's through on goal!» What is the commentator doing? | *Describing the match as it happens | Ordering a pizza | Measuring the pitch | Writing a shopping list
exercise: «She is a political commentator on the news.» Which word tells you what topic she talks about? | is | she | *political | commentator
test: «The sports commentator shouted as the striker scored.» What is the commentator doing? | *Describing the goal as it happens | Asking for a drink | Reading a book quietly | Sleeping in the stand
test: Which sentence gives an opinion? | «The match was held on Saturday.» | «Ten thousand people came to watch.» | «The score was two goals to one.» | *«The referee was clearly wrong to give that penalty.»
exam: What does commentator mean in «a running commentary on the cricket»? | A cricket bat | *Someone who describes the cricket as it happens | A person who sleeps in the pavilion | A type of cricket ball
